verdicts.reason:
The decomposition is wrong. B counts the 0.078 s unattributed CPU as support. Per bench/CHANGELOG.md:151-156 and bench/report.py:323-325, unattributed is CPU the 10 ms sampler loses (threads ending between samples, below each thread's last tick), mostly the workers'.

Per round in r41980640481, the gap (median 0.0734 s) splits as:
- attributed support (scanner + main): 53.4% [35.7-60.7];
- unattributed: 26.0% [17.9-36.8];
- sampler: 2.1%;
- idle: 15.6% [12.3-45.0].

The bottom line survives. About 80% of the gap is real CPU and grows with bytes wherever it is attributed, so wall_n is the better reading. But wall_n also scales up the fixed idle (about 1.4-1.7% of capacity, measured on the 9V74, not this runner) and the sampler (0.45%, absent from a release). The model's workers_ns_per_out_byte (5.055) and scanner_binds_from (7.86) are understated by the unattributed worker CPU.

The saturation half survives, recomputed from 41980640481 runs.jsonl (Xeon 8573C), wikidata, mibz2 arm, 4t, 10 rounds: wall 0.3426 s, CPU 1.3139 s, median ratio 0.961 (range 0.855-0.970). The occupancy run agrees: decoding 93.0%, 3.72 of 4 (41976148952, EPYC 7763).

The 'scheduling' half does not survive. The 3.9% bounds idle time only. Scheduling also moves the larger term, CPU per block under SMT co-run:
- #180, a pure scheduling change, raised 4t CPU by 4.3-6.1% (window.md:102-104, 114-117);
- packed against spread at 2t was +40% (four-thread-ceiling.md:51-53);
- forced teams ran 0.71x.
The co-run term is about 1 - 1/1.62 = 38% of 4t CPU (OBSERVED 1.634x amplification from the same runs.jsonl). No measurement bounds what co-run-aware placement could recover from it.

There are pre-#180 counterexamples:
- #170 run 2 (EPYC 7763): 4t wall −1.9% (−3.6, −0.2) with CPU −2.0% (−3.3, −0.7) (mtf-short-runs.md:60);
- #172 run 1: CPU −2.2%, wall −2.2%;
- #171 itself gained 4t wall.

The rejections the front would flip did not fail on CPU-to-wall. They failed because the 1t gain never became a 4t CPU gain:
- #25: 1t CPU −1.7%, 4t CPU −0.6% (ns), on bench 1.0.0, whose arm order favoured head by about 2% (early-warning.md:104-121);
- #114: 4t CPU +1.1%.

#180 does not touch that link. After #180, #183 on EPYC 9V45 had 1t CPU −2.5% (−4.1, −0.8) and 4t CPU +1.0% (−3.8, +6.1) (artifact 13396557790).

CPU ≈ wall at saturation is supported (INFERRED from 0.961). The history claim and its corollary are not.
